      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Coronary artery bypass surgery is an accepted treatment for patients with coronary artery disease. Perioperative morbidity includes development of supraventricular arrhythmias. To prevent this, prophylactic administration of drugs such as calcium channel blockers, digoxin, and beta-blockers have been advised."},
